---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="A support bot answers from a 7-document help centre. Change how it chunks, retrieves and packs the prompt, and see whether the right passage arrives.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Start as is (30 word chunks, no overlap, top-3): the verdict is <b>Wrong chunk</b>. The right page is retrieved, but its accessories chunk (14 days) outranks the chunk with the laptop sentence. Set <b>overlap</b> to 10 and it becomes <b>Grounded</b>. Top-k 5 also works, but 3 of the 5 chunks are off-topic and the prompt grows from 135 to 210 tokens.</li>
    <li>Press <b>Reset</b>, then set chunk size 40: <b>Split</b>, because a boundary cuts the sentence and one half arrived. Top-k 5 brings both halves (<b>Fragmented</b>, 227 tokens). Chunk size 60 keeps the sentence whole: <b>Grounded</b>.</li>
    <li>Press <b>Reset</b>, then set chunk size 20, overlap 10, top-k 5: <b>Split</b>. Tick <b>Rerank</b> and the right chunks climb into the top 5: <b>Grounded</b>. Back at the defaults, <b>Query rewrite</b> also fixes it, because "send back" never matches the word "return" lexically.</li>
    <li>Press <b>Reset</b>, then tick <b>Stale 2023 copy still indexed</b>: at the defaults the old 14 day policy wins (<b>Stale</b>); at chunk size 60 both versions arrive (<b>Conflict</b>). Untick it, set chunk size 60 and budget 100: the right chunk is found but <b>cut by the budget</b>.</li>
    <li>Press <b>Reset</b>, untick <b>Filter by user permissions</b>, then set chunk size 60, top-k 5 and budget 400: a staff-only chunk reaches the prompt (<b>Leak</b>). Tick <b>Filter by user permissions</b> again and switch to the drone question: nothing in the corpus answers it, yet a chunk is retrieved (<b>Hallucination risk</b>). Set <b>abstain below</b> to 50 and the bot says it does not know; at 150 on the laptop question it wrongly gives up.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg rag" data-rag>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Question <select class="pg-in" data-q><option value="laptop" selected>How long can I send back a laptop after delivery?</option><option value="drone">What is the refund window for a drone? (not in the corpus)</option></select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Chunk size (words) <input type="range" min="20" max="120" step="10" value="30" data-size /> <b data-sizeval>30</b></label>
      <label>Overlap (words) <input type="range" min="0" max="40" step="10" value="0" data-overlap /> <b data-overlapval>0</b></label>
      <label>Top-k <input type="range" min="1" max="6" step="1" value="3" data-k /> <b data-kval>3</b></label>
      <label>Token budget <input type="range" min="60" max="400" step="20" value="240" data-budget /> <b data-budgetval>240</b></label>
      <label>Abstain below score <input type="range" min="0" max="160" step="10" value="0" data-min /> <b data-minval>0 (off)</b></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label class="rag-check"><input type="checkbox" data-rerank /> Rerank</label>
      <label class="rag-check"><input type="checkbox" data-rewrite /> Query rewrite</label>
      <label class="rag-check"><input type="checkbox" data-stale /> Stale 2023 copy still indexed</label>
      <label class="rag-check"><input type="checkbox" checked data-acl /> Filter by user permissions</label>
      <button class="btn" type="button" data-reset>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-verdictbox aria-live="polite"><h3>Verdict</h3><span data-verdict></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-3)"><h3>Prompt budget</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-tokens></span><div class="rag-meter" aria-hidden="true"><div class="rag-fill" data-fill></div></div><span class="pg-note" data-noise></span></div>
    </div>
    <h3 class="rag-h">Ranked chunks</h3>
    <ol class="rag-rows" data-rows aria-label="Ranked chunks, best first"></ol>
    <p class="pg-mono" data-stats></p>
    <details class="rag-corpus">
      <summary>The corpus (7 documents, tokens are estimated as 1.3 per word plus 6 for the citation header)</summary>
      <ul>
        <li>Returns policy (current): accessories 14 days, laptops 30 days</li>
        <li>Returns policy 2023 (stale): laptops 14 days</li>
        <li>Shipping and delivery, Laptop warranty: similar words, different topic</li>
        <li>Internal refund exceptions (staff only): 60 days for enterprise</li>
        <li>Payments, Your account: unrelated</li>
      </ul>
    </details>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, numberValue } from '../playground';
  interface Doc { id: string; title: string; flag: string; text: string; answer?: string }
  interface Chunk { id: string; doc: string; flag: string; start: number; words: string[]; stems: string[]; score: number }
  interface Opts { answerable: boolean; query: string; size: number; overlap: number; k: number; rerank: boolean; rewrite: boolean; budget: number; stale: boolean; acl: boolean; minScore: number }
  const DOCS: Doc[] = [
  { id: "returns", title: "Returns policy", flag: "", text: "Returns policy. Customers may return unused accessories such as cables and cases within 14 days of delivery. Opened software cannot be refunded. Refunds go back to the original payment method within 5 business days. Returns of laptops are accepted within 30 days of delivery if the device works and all original packaging is included. Gift purchases can be returned for store credit only." , answer: "laptops are accepted within 30 days of delivery" },
  { id: "shipping", title: "Shipping and delivery", flag: "", text: "Shipping and delivery. Standard delivery takes 3 to 5 days and express delivery takes 1 to 2 days. A laptop ships in a padded box and needs a signature on delivery. After delivery you can track the parcel for 30 days. Delivery to islands can take 10 days." },
  { id: "warranty", title: "Laptop warranty", flag: "", text: "Laptop warranty. The warranty covers defects for 12 months after delivery. To claim, send the laptop back to a service centre with the order number. We repair or replace the laptop within 21 days. Damage from liquids is not covered." },
  { id: "returns2023", title: "Returns policy 2023", flag: "stale", text: "Returns policy 2023. Customers may return unused accessories within 14 days of delivery. Returns of laptops are accepted within 14 days of delivery if the device works and all original packaging is included. Refunds go back to the original payment method.", answer: "laptops are accepted within 14 days of delivery" },
  { id: "exceptions", title: "Internal refund exceptions", flag: "restricted", text: "Internal refund exceptions for support staff only. Enterprise customers may return a laptop up to 60 days after delivery with manager approval. Never share this table with consumers." },
  { id: "payments", title: "Payments", flag: "", text: "Payments. We accept cards and bank transfer. Invoices are due in 30 days. A failed payment is retried twice before the order is cancelled." },
  { id: "account", title: "Your account", flag: "", text: "Your account. Reset your password from the sign in page. You can export your order history as a file. Closing an account deletes saved addresses." },
  ];
  const QUERIES: Record<string, { text: string; answerable: boolean }> = {
    laptop: { text: 'how long can I send back a laptop after delivery', answerable: true },
    drone: { text: 'what is the refund window for a drone', answerable: false },
  };
  const MIN_STEM_LEN = 3; // words this short keep a trailing s
  const IDF_SCALE = 4096; // fixed-point scale for the idf ratio
  const TOK_PER_10_WORDS = 13; const CHUNK_OVERHEAD_TOK = 6; // about 1.3 tokens per word, plus a header per chunk
  const RERANK_WINDOW = 12; // words in the sliding window the reranker scores
  const TF_CAP = 2; // repeats of a term beyond this add nothing
  const RERANK_POOL = 8; const RERANK_WEIGHT = 4; // candidates reranked; window score weight against the first score
  const MIN_STEP = 10; // overlap must leave each chunk at least this many new words
  const STOP = new Set('how can i a an the of to is are in on and or for after you your with by it'.split(' '));
  const stem = (w: string) => (w.length > MIN_STEM_LEN && w.endsWith('s') ? w.slice(0, -1) : w);
  const words = (t: string) => t.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9 ]/g, ' ').split(' ').filter(Boolean);
  const terms = (q: string) => [...new Set(words(q).filter((w) => !STOP.has(w)).map(stem))];
  const wide = (ts: string[]) => [...new Set([...ts, 'return', 'day'])];
  const bitlen = (x: number) => { let n = 0; while (x > 0) { n++; x = Math.floor(x / 2); } return n; };
  // idf as a fixed-point log2 in half steps: 2 x the bit length plus the next bit
  function idfOf(n: number, df: number) { const x = Math.floor((IDF_SCALE * n) / df); const b = bitlen(x) - 1; return 2 * b + (b >= 1 ? Math.floor(x / 2 ** (b - 1)) % 2 : 0); }
  const tokensOf = (w: number) => Math.floor((w * TOK_PER_10_WORDS + 9) / 10) + CHUNK_OVERHEAD_TOK; // tenths rounded up

  function chunkAll(docs: Doc[], size: number, overlap: number): Chunk[] {
    const out: Chunk[] = [];
    for (const d of docs) {
      const w = words(d.text); const step = size - overlap; let n = 0;
      for (let s = 0; s < w.length; s += step) {
        const part = w.slice(s, s + size);
        out.push({ id: `${d.id}#${n++}`, doc: d.id, flag: d.flag, start: s, words: part, stems: part.map(stem), score: 0 });
        if (s + size >= w.length) break;
      }
    }
    return out;
  }
  function windowScore(stems: string[], ts: string[], idf: Record<string, number>, win = RERANK_WINDOW) {
    let best = 0;
    for (let s = 0; s < stems.length; s++) { let sc = 0; const part = stems.slice(s, s + win); for (const t of ts) if (part.includes(t)) sc += idf[t] ?? 0; if (sc > best) best = sc; }
    return best;
  }
  function run(o: Opts) {
    const docs = DOCS.filter((d) => o.stale || d.flag !== 'stale');
    const chunks = chunkAll(docs, o.size, o.overlap);
    const base = terms(o.query); const ext = wide(base); const ts = o.rewrite ? ext : base;
    const idf: Record<string, number> = {};
    for (const t of ext) { const df = chunks.filter((c) => c.stems.includes(t)).length; if (df) idf[t] = idfOf(chunks.length, df); }
    const allowed = chunks.filter((c) => !(o.acl && c.flag === 'restricted'));
    for (const c of allowed) { c.score = 0; for (const t of ts) { const tf = c.stems.filter((x) => x === t).length; if (tf) c.score += (idf[t] ?? 0) * Math.min(tf, TF_CAP); } }
    const byScore = (a: Chunk, b: Chunk) => b.score - a.score || (a.id < b.id ? -1 : 1);
    let ranked = allowed.filter((c) => c.score > 0).sort(byScore);
    const firstTop = ranked.length ? ranked[0].score : 0;
    if (o.rerank) { const cand = ranked.slice(0, RERANK_POOL); for (const c of cand) c.score = windowScore(c.stems, ext, idf) * RERANK_WEIGHT + Math.floor(c.score / RERANK_WEIGHT); ranked = cand.sort(byScore); }
    const top = ranked.slice(0, o.k);
    const ctx: Chunk[] = []; const dropped: Chunk[] = []; let used = 0;
    for (const c of top) { const t = tokensOf(c.words.length); if (used + t <= o.budget) { ctx.push(c); used += t; } else dropped.push(c); }
    return { chunks, ranked, top, ctx, used, dropped, firstTop };
  }
  type Result = ReturnType<typeof run>;
  const phrase = (id: string) => words(DOCS.find((d) => d.id === id)!.answer!).map(stem);
  function hasPhrase(c: Chunk, a: string[]) { for (let i = 0; i + a.length <= c.stems.length; i++) if (a.every((w, j) => c.stems[i + j] === w)) return true; return false; }
  function verdict(o: Opts, r: Result): ['good' | 'bad', string] {
    const cur = phrase('returns'); const old = phrase('returns2023');
    const leak = r.ctx.some((c) => c.flag === 'restricted');
    const abstain = o.minScore > 0 && r.firstTop < o.minScore;
    if (leak) return ['bad', 'Leak: a staff-only chunk is in the prompt. Filter by permission before retrieval.'];
    if (!o.answerable) {
      if (abstain || r.ctx.length === 0) return ['good', 'Correct no-answer: the corpus has no drone policy and the system says so.'];
      return ['bad', `Hallucination risk: nothing answers this, but ${r.ctx.length} plausible chunk(s) are in the prompt.`];
    }
    if (abstain) return ['bad', `Over-abstained: the answer is in the corpus, but the top score ${r.firstTop} is under the threshold ${o.minScore}.`];
    const good = r.ctx.some((c) => c.doc === 'returns' && hasPhrase(c, cur));
    const stale = r.ctx.some((c) => c.doc === 'returns2023' && hasPhrase(c, old));
    const goodDropped = r.dropped.some((c) => c.doc === 'returns' && hasPhrase(c, cur));
    const parts = r.ctx.filter((c) => c.doc === 'returns');
    const tail = parts.some((c) => { for (let i = 1; i < cur.length; i++) if (cur.slice(0, i).every((w, j) => c.stems[c.stems.length - i + j] === w)) return true; return false; });
    const head = parts.some((c) => { for (let i = 1; i < cur.length; i++) if (cur.slice(i).every((w, j) => c.stems[j] === w)) return true; return false; });
    if (good && stale) return ['bad', 'Conflict: the current 30 day and the stale 14 day answers are both in the prompt.'];
    if (good) return ['good', 'Grounded: the complete 30 day sentence is in the prompt, so the answer can cite it.'];
    if (stale) return ['bad', 'Stale: the model will confidently cite the 14 day 2023 policy.'];
    if (goodDropped) return ['bad', 'Retrieved but cut: the right chunk did not fit the token budget.'];
    if (tail && head) return ['bad', 'Fragmented: both halves of the sentence are in the prompt as separate chunks. The model must stitch them.'];
    if (tail || head) return ['bad', 'Split: a chunk boundary cut the answer sentence and only one half reached the prompt.'];
    if (parts.length) return ['bad', 'Wrong chunk: the returns page was retrieved, but the chunk is the accessories (14 day) part, not the laptop sentence.'];
    return ['bad', 'Wrong passages: similar shipping or warranty text, no returns chunk.'];
  }

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-rag]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const num = numberValue(q);
    const chk = (s: string) => q<HTMLInputElement>(s).checked;
    const ROWS = 6;
    const rows: { li: HTMLElement; head: HTMLElement; tag: HTMLElement; text: HTMLElement }[] = [];
    const list = q('[data-rows]');
    for (let i = 0; i < ROWS; i++) {
      const li = document.createElement('li'); li.className = 'rag-row';
      const head = document.createElement('span'); head.className = 'pg-mono rag-head';
      const tag = document.createElement('b'); tag.className = 'rag-tag';
      const text = document.createElement('span'); text.className = 'pg-note rag-text';
      li.append(head, tag, text); list.appendChild(li); rows.push({ li, head, tag, text });
    }
    let raf = 0;
    function opts(): Opts {
      const size = num('[data-size]'); const overlap = Math.min(num('[data-overlap]'), size - MIN_STEP);
      const qq = QUERIES[q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-q]').value];
      return { answerable: qq.answerable, query: qq.text, size, overlap, k: num('[data-k]'), rerank: chk('[data-rerank]'), rewrite: chk('[data-rewrite]'), budget: num('[data-budget]'), stale: chk('[data-stale]'), acl: chk('[data-acl]'), minScore: num('[data-min]') };
    }
    function draw() {
      raf = 0;
      const o = opts(); const r = run(o); const [kind, msg] = verdict(o, r);
      q('[data-sizeval]').textContent = String(o.size);
      q('[data-overlapval]').textContent = String(o.overlap);
      q('[data-kval]').textContent = String(o.k);
      q('[data-budgetval]').textContent = String(o.budget);
      q('[data-minval]').textContent = o.minScore ? String(o.minScore) : '0 (off)';
      q('[data-verdict]').textContent = msg;
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-verdictbox]').style.setProperty('--c', kind === 'good' ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      q('[data-tokens]').textContent = `${r.used} of ${o.budget} tokens used`;
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-fill]').style.width = `${Math.min(100, Math.round((r.used / o.budget) * 100))}%`;
      const off = r.ctx.filter((c) => c.doc !== 'returns' && c.doc !== 'returns2023').length;
      q('[data-noise]').textContent = r.ctx.length ? `${off} of ${r.ctx.length} chunks in the prompt are off-topic` : 'no chunk in the prompt';
      const shown = r.ranked.slice(0, ROWS);
      rows.forEach((row, i) => {
        const c = shown[i]; row.li.hidden = !c; if (!c) return;
        const inCtx = r.ctx.includes(c); const cut = r.dropped.includes(c);
        const status = inCtx ? 'in prompt' : cut ? 'cut by budget' : 'below top-k';
        const flag = c.flag ? ` · ${c.flag}` : '';
        row.head.textContent = `${i + 1}. ${c.id} · score ${c.score} · ${tokensOf(c.words.length)} tok${flag}`;
        row.tag.textContent = status;
        row.text.textContent = c.words.join(' ');
        row.li.dataset.status = inCtx ? 'in' : cut ? 'cut' : 'out';
      });
      q('[data-stats]').textContent = `index: ${r.chunks.length} chunks · matched: ${r.ranked.length} · first-stage top score: ${r.firstTop}${o.rerank ? ' · reranked the best 8' : ''}`;
    }
    const schedule = () => { if (!raf) raf = window.requestAnimationFrame(draw); };
    root.addEventListener('input', schedule); root.addEventListener('change', schedule);
    q('[data-reset]').addEventListener('click', () => {
      q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-q]').value = 'laptop';
      ([['[data-size]', '30'], ['[data-overlap]', '0'], ['[data-k]', '3'], ['[data-budget]', '240'], ['[data-min]', '0']] as const).forEach(([s, v]) => { q<HTMLInputElement>(s).value = v; });
      q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-rerank]').checked = false; q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-rewrite]').checked = false; q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-stale]').checked = false; q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-acl]').checked = true;
      draw();
    });
    draw();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .rag-check { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
  .playground .rag-h { margin: 4px 0 0; font-size: 1rem; }
  .playground .rag-meter { height: 8px; border-radius: 4px; background: var(--surface-2); border: 1px solid var(--border); overflow: hidden; }
  .playground .rag-fill { height: 100%; background: var(--role-3); width: 0; }
  .playground .rag-rows { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 8px; }
  .playground .rag-row { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 6px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 6px 10px; background: var(--surface); display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 10px; align-items: baseline; }
  .playground .rag-row[hidden] { display: none; }
  .playground .rag-row[data-status="in"] { border-left-color: var(--good); }
  .playground .rag-row[data-status="cut"] { border-left-color: var(--bad); }
  .playground .rag-row[data-status="out"] { border-style: dashed; border-left-style: solid; }
  .playground .rag-tag { font-size: .8rem; }
  .playground .rag-text { flex-basis: 100%; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .playground .rag-corpus { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--muted); }
</style>
